From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ugur-imd <ugur.acikgoz@imd-tec.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:10:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: imdt-v2-sbc: stop back-feeding VBUS on the USB2
 OTG port

The 6.1 device tree rework pointed usb2_phy0's vbus-supply at the PHY's
internal vbus-regulator. The driver enables that regulator at probe and
can only switch it off again for a GPIO-controlled supply, so VBUS stays
on even when the board is the USB device. The host on the other end (a
PC, or the LAVA worker) then sees VBUS back-feed and trips its
over-current protection. Both the V2H and the V2N do this.

Disable the internal regulator and give the PHY a plain fixed supply
instead. The PHY then drives VBUS through VBOUT according to the OTG
role, as it did on dunfell: off as a device, on as a host.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/imdt-v2-sbc.dtsi | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/imdt-v2-sbc.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/imdt-v2-sbc.dtsi
index 8b0e86b..29336e0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/imdt-v2-sbc.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/imdt-v2-sbc.dtsi
@@ -37,6 +37,14 @@
 		};
 	};
 
+	/* VBUS on the OTG port is switched by the PHY itself (VBOUT), per role. */
+	usb20_vbus: regulator-usb20-vbus {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "usb20-vbus";
+		regulator-min-microvolt = <5000000>;
+		regulator-max-microvolt = <5000000>;
+	};
+
 	reg_1p8v: regulator0 {
 		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
 
@@ -797,15 +805,21 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/*
+ * The PHY's internal vbus-regulator is switched on at probe and the driver
+ * cannot switch it off again, so the board back-feeds VBUS into the host it
+ * is attached to as a device. Use a plain supply instead, so VBUS follows
+ * the OTG role as it did on dunfell.
+ */
 &usb2_phy0_vbus_otg {
-	status = "okay";
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 
 &usb2_phy0 {
 	pinctrl-0 = <&usb20_pins>;
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 
-	vbus-supply = <&usb2_phy0_vbus_otg>;
+	vbus-supply = <&usb20_vbus>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
-- 
